{"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},{"type":"text","text":" and the store’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" effect or the imperative "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Identity lives outside the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" type — it is still a plain closure — so nothing about reducer signatures changes."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Choosing an id","anchor":"Choosing-an-id","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["private enum SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private enum SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to tag the work, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the speaking effect is cancelled, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop ends at the next suspension point, exactly as it would on teardown."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancelInFlight: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code","type":"heading","text":"Cancel from view or scene code"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" directly:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace","type":"heading","text":"What it does not replace"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"defer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Cancellation ends the task; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}]},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Cancel Effects"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","title":"Add Feature Flags"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","title":"Add a Version Killswitch"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","role":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.cancel(id:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancellable"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"cancelInFlight"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Cancels every in-flight effect tagged with ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","title":"cancel(id:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","role":"article","title":"Add iCloud Sync","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":" with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cancelEffects","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"cancelEffects()","abstract":[{"text":"Cancels all in-flight effects.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancel(id:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An effect that cancels every in-flight effect running under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6Effecta","text":"Effect"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","title":"cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancel(id:)"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","role":"article","title":"Add Analytics","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","title":"Add a Paywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","role":"article","title":"Add a Parental Gate","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Effect","abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":" plugin and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" macro — no hand-written ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"text":" classes, database actors, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","title":"Add Persistence"}}}